.TH SEAL 1 "2025" "ChonkOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
seal \- configuration snapshots of tracked system files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seal
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-store " PATH" ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seal
records and restores snapshots ("seals") of tracked configuration files.
Snapshots live in
.I /var/lib/chonkos/seals/<id>/
as manifest.json, file copies under files/, and packages.txt. Exit status is
0 on success and 1 on any error.
Tracked paths: /etc/apt/sources.list, /etc/apt/sources.list.d,
/etc/default/zramswap, /etc/fstab, /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d,
/etc/xdg/fastfetch, /etc/sysctl.d. Symlinks and secret-looking file names
(components ending in _key, .pem or .key) are excluded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a table.
.TP
.BI \-\-store " PATH"
Use PATH as the snapshot store instead of /var/lib/chonkos/seals.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR mark " MESSAGE"
Create a snapshot with ID <UTC timestamp>-<slug>; stores SHA-256 per tracked
file and the manually installed packages (apt-mark showmanual).
.TP
.B list
List snapshots, newest first.
.TP
.BR diff " [\fIID\fR]"
Compare the system with the given snapshot (default: latest).
.TP
.BR restore " ID TARGET_PATH [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]"
Restore one tracked absolute path from a snapshot; an existing file is backed
up to <name>.bak.<timestamp> and the restored content is checksum-verified.
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR only verifies.
.TP
.BR export " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Write a JSON system profile (manual packages, OS name/version, tracked file
hashes) to FILE or stdout.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
seal mark "before upgrade"
.TP
seal list
.TP
seal diff
.TP
sudo seal restore 20250101-120000-before-upgrade /etc/fstab --dry-run
.TP
seal export /root/profile.json
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/chonkos/seals/
Default snapshot store.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chonk (1)
